sections.content:
HQL (Hive Query Language) is an SQL-like language used to create, retrieve, modify and manage data stored in Hive.
Commands: CREATE (creates database or table), LOAD (loads data), SELECT (retrieves records), INSERT (inserts records), UPDATE/DELETE (modify or delete records where supported), DROP (removes database or table).
Example:
```sql
CREATE TABLE students (roll_no INT, name STRING, department STRING);
SELECT * FROM students;
INSERT INTO students VALUES (101, 'Raja', 'AI&DS');
```

